# Alert 1 – High CPU Load

## Alert

```text
Warning
system.cpu.load.5min is 10.9

Load 1 min  : 12.64
Load 5 min  : 10.92
Load 15 min : 6.80

```

---

## Investigation

Verified CPU utilization.

```bash
top/htop
uptime
```

Checked processes consuming CPU.

```bash
ps -eo pid,ppid,user,%cpu,%mem,cmd --sort=-%cpu | head
```

Observed continuous PostgreSQL queries consuming CPU resources.
Checked PostgreSQL activity.

```sql
SELECT pid,state,query
FROM pg_stat_activity;
```
Or if any other application processes consuming cpu that checked with concern application teaam.

Verified disk I/O to determine whether CPU load was caused by I/O wait.

```bash
iostat -xz 1 5
vmstat 1 5
```

---

## Root Cause

Continuous PostgreSQL queries increased CPU utilization.
In some cases, elevated **I/O wait** due to storage latency also contributed to higher system load.
Or application process increase the load due to bugs or high traffic.

---

## Resolution

* Verified running PostgreSQL queries.
* Shared query details with the Database/Operations team.
* Recommended query optimization.
* Monitored CPU load until it returned to normal.
* If high I/O wait was observed, storage performance was investigated before escalating.

---

## Skills Demonstrated

* Linux Performance Tuning
* PostgreSQL Monitoring
* CPU Analysis
* I/O Wait Analysis
* Cross-Team Coordination

