# Alert 5 – Memory Degraded (Hardware) / Memory issue on HPE/DELL servers

## Alert

```text
Memroy usage high alerts on servers
ILO resilient memory condition Degraded
```

---

## Investigation


Verified host memory usage.
Checked VMware memory statistics.

Reviewed:

* Memory Pressure
* Ballooning
* Swapping
* Overhead Memory

Verified DIMM health through the server management interface.

---

## Root Cause

The was caused by a hardware memory fault. HPE iLO logs recorded an Uncorrectable ECC memory error and the affected module 
(PROC 1 DIMM 12) was placed in Map Out Configuration, indicating the firmware disabled the faulty DIMM. The server automatically reset and 
recovered using Automatic Power Recovery. No PSOD, kernel panic, or ESXi software fault was found in the vmkernel logs.

---

## Resolution

When memory pressure was the issue:

* Migrated virtual machines to another ESXi host using VMware vMotion.
* Reduced resource contention.
* Monitored host memory after migration.

When hardware degradation was confirmed:

* Prepared a Method of Procedure (MOP).
* Scheduled DIMM replacement during the maintenance window.
* Verified server health after replacement.

---

## Skills Demonstrated

* VMware Administration
* Capacity Management
* Hardware Troubleshooting
* Memory Analysis

